arXiv:2609.17551v1 Announce Type: new 
Abstract: Bilu and Linial conjectured that if $d\ge 2$, then every $d$-regular graph $G$ has an edge signing $\sigma:E(G)\to\{-1,1\}$ such that its signed adjacency matrix $A_\sigma$ satisfies the Ramanujan bound \begin{equation*}
  \rho(A_\sigma)\le 2\sqrt{d-1} \end{equation*} and they proved that \begin{equation*}
  \rho(A_\sigma)=O\!\left(\sqrt{d\log^3 d}\right). \end{equation*}
  Using a method of interlacing polynomials, Marcus, Spielman, and Srivastav
